Q: Navigation bar positioning A: <p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="false" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Homepage&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;style type="text/css"&gt;
html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }

#container
{
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: #FFF;
    width: 100%;
}

header
{
    height: 180px;
    padding: 1% 1%;
    background-color: #22272A;
    margin: 0 auto;
}

title
{
    color: #FFF;
    margin: 0 auto;
    position: absolute;
    left: 20%;
    top: 2%;
    font-size: 48px;
    font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;
}

nav { position: relative; }         
nav ul { display: inline-block; }       
nav ul li
{
    list-style: none;
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    float: left;
    padding: 10px;
    text-align: center;
}

nav ul li .active
{
    color: #3479FA;
    background: #FFF; 
    border: 1px solid white;
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 10px;
}

nav ul li a
{
    text-decoration: none;
    color: #FFF;
    line-height: 30px;
    width: 40px;    
}
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;

&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;div id="container"&gt;
        &lt;header&gt;
            &lt;title&gt;Sample Text&lt;/title&gt;
            &lt;nav&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li class="active"&gt;&lt;a href="bla.html" class="active"&gt;bla&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="bla.html"&gt;bla&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/nav&gt;
        &lt;/header&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: How can I place text boxes on the same line while allowing responsive widths longer than the browser default? A: <p>If I understand your question correctly, then by placing <code>input</code> in a <code>flex</code> container with <code>flex-direction: column</code> and adding <code>max-width: 100%</code> to it - you will get the desired result:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>* {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

.input-group {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;
}

.input {
  max-width: 100%;
}

.input-big {
  width: 20rem;
}

.input-small {
  width: 5rem;
}

.input-block {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-start;
  min-width: 0;
}

.input-title {
  max-width: 100%;
  white-space: nowrap;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="input-group"&gt;
    &lt;label class="input-block"&gt;
        &lt;span class="input-title"&gt;First Name&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;input type="text" class="input input-big" /&gt;
    &lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;label class="input-block"&gt;
        &lt;span class="input-title"&gt;Last Name&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;input type="text" class="input input-small" /&gt;
    &lt;/label&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="input-group"&gt;
    &lt;label class="input-block"&gt;
        &lt;span class="input-title"&gt;Last Name&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;input type="text" class="input input-small" /&gt;
    &lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;label class="input-block"&gt;
        &lt;span class="input-title"&gt;First Name&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;input type="text" class="input input-big" /&gt;
    &lt;/label&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
